CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ virtual call: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
too many addressed objects
--
The virtual tables of classes that are never constructed were initialized,
so each of their virtual functions was an addressed object: 100 unused
classes exceed the 256 objects of the default --object-bits 8.  With
libc++ the locale facets declared through <vector> had the same effect.
